; Copy the name phrase of an object or place into a record buffer
;
; Copies the six bytes of the name phrase (noun and two adjectives) of object B,
; or of place B when the kind in A is not 0, to DE. B = $FF means no noun and
; nothing is copied. Called by #R$7AF5 for RecBuf1 ($7942) and RecBuf2
; ($7948) so that a command given to a character carries its noun phrases.
;
; A Noun kind (Noun1Kind or Noun2Kind): 0 object, else location
; B Object or location id, $FF for none
; DE Where to copy to
; O:BC 0 (when copied)
; O:DE After the copy (when copied)
; O:HL After the name phrase (when copied)
@label=CopyNamePhrase
c$7B63 INC B         ;
 $7B64 RET Z         ; $FF: none
 $7B65 DEC B         ;
 $7B66 AND A         ;
 $7B67 LD A,B        ;
 $7B68 JR Z,$7B6F    ;
 $7B6A CALL $71D5    ; LocationNamePtr
 $7B6D JR $7B72      ;
*$7B6F CALL $71E2    ; ObjectNamePtr
@isub=LD BC,PHRASE_WORDS_SIZE
*$7B72 LD BC,$0006   ;
 $7B75 LDIR          ;
 $7B77 RET           ;
